#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087412 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ec37c5e-8a40-58a7-8af3-4457cd5da43f" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions"}] :question/id #uuid "7826cd52-8603-51ff-902e-c7764639dccd" :question/math-academy-id "e-3666" :question/problem "Express $\\cos^2{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)} - \\sin^2{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x - \\sin^2 x = \\cos 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24})-{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{24}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{24}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{12}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087413 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12ff17ae-9319-5498-a5e0-1d49ddbef50a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Alternative Forms of Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions"}] :question/id #uuid "2b9dc462-ec26-5762-aa64-d9e8f16112c9" :question/math-academy-id "e-3667" :question/problem "Express $2\\cos^2{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right)}-1$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n2 \\cos^2 x - 1 = \\cos 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-1 & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087414 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2902b205-4508-55c6-9a68-f57d3afc9eab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values of Trigonometric Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/id #uuid "e617aaf2-1232-57cc-8644-2467effda030" :question/math-academy-id "e-3668" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\cos^2\\left( 22.5^\\circ\\right) - \\sin^2\\left( 22.5^\\circ\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x - \\sin^2 x = \\cos 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={22.5^\\circ}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡({22.5}^{∘})-{sin}^{2}⁡({22.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {22.5}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ec37c5e-8a40-58a7-8af3-4457cd5da43f" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aea59c7-4ab1-557d-bb3b-d1d0c9e5550f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262370} {:answer/id #uuid "c2b65bde-469c-58e0-bd06-c2fe18633322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262371} {:answer/id #uuid "83b02bf6-5f6b-5777-a038-55a1901e61bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262372} {:answer/id #uuid "25d9d878-cf74-5cb7-9d94-4e75ec4289ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262373} {:answer/id #uuid "1edd5c16-fb61-5348-be7f-3dc177df7d8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25d9d878-cf74-5cb7-9d94-4e75ec4289ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262373} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7ce1c18-794c-59f4-bcce-c19d9799a8f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0194f2b8-4c4e-5a5b-b724-7a12e1903c33" :question/math-academy-id "q-120348" :question/problem "Express $\\sqrt{3}{cos}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}-\\sqrt{3}{sin}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}({cos}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={35}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {35}^{∘})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}({cos}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡{35}^{∘})=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ec37c5e-8a40-58a7-8af3-4457cd5da43f" :knowledge-point/title "Using the Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e54b9eea-52ba-5811-baed-9d73f42cf70d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{38}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302058} {:answer/id #uuid "e35f836c-4994-5507-be3c-d59065b10013" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{76}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302059} {:answer/id #uuid "7b14610f-fc44-5244-a0f7-088c25899a6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{76}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302060} {:answer/id #uuid "e00d5b9f-dec9-5faa-a21d-1787bc1e4e21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{76}^{∘}" :