#edb/ref 17592186085171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eda88667-03a3-54d2-bc45-5bd8cd910c52" :question/math-academy-id "q-24488" :question/problem "Express ${cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})-{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088053 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2902b205-4508-55c6-9a68-f57d3afc9eab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values of Trigonometric Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c2f1518-b867-508f-a628-2bab10b49f02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085244} {:answer/id #uuid "9b5b3a95-e4e1-531a-99de-1a099743ff5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085245} {:answer/id #uuid "c0621b26-38d0-5c29-934d-af0129b4b066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085246} {:answer/id #uuid "d6cd6dab-4fd7-569d-ae98-491c9f64372e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085247} {:answer/id #uuid "27f96a95-45f7-5146-86d2-ee94f7e5bf3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085248}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b5b3a95-e4e1-531a-99de-1a099743ff5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085245} :answer-field/id #uuid "24ff6ca5-a746-5722-96d9-94e859d81d7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085243}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0283435-c23b-5d26-b5af-8d4a513ca18b" :question/math-academy-id "q-26706" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $1-2{sin}^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={67.5}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2{sin}^{2}⁡({67.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {67.5}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{135}^{∘} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302077 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2902b205-4508-55c6-9a68-f57d3afc9eab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values of Trigonometric Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2e4e5ee-8f2a-5b25-9c4a-69ddbde50454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302079} {:answer/id #uuid "f6cd7bcb-3de1-541c-bb53-94df1808b15f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6cd7bcb-3de1-541c-bb53-94df1808b15f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302080} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce2ecf3a-4132-54d3-bf34-3e4322776b8a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ba3ee242-53d3-59bb-9592-b216b9936095" :question/math-academy-id "q-332150" :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of the expression below.\n\n${cos}^{4}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})-2{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}){sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})+{sin}^{4}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that our expression is a perfect square that can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{4}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})-2{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}){sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})+{sin}^{4}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}) & ={({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}))}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{12}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}) & =cos\\,(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =cos\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12})-{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{7\\pi }{12}))}^{2} & ={(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302081 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12ff17ae-9319-5498-a5e0-1d49ddbef50a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Alternative Forms of Double-Angle Formula to Simplify Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edbbed19-24ff-5d8f-8ad8-905657c615ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{84}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302083} {:answer/id #uuid "53e7dcec-e159-56dc-8dbf-016a35793188" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡{52}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302084} {:answer/id #uuid "ae16619e-c43c-53af-9872-ac4a562606dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{84}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302085} {:answer/id #uuid "048616dc-8ddc-5180-aa34-d4ee381abaa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{42}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302086} {:answer/id #uuid "18f9cf39-1c67-5248-b538-431cec4908ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{84}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18f9cf39-1c67-5248-b538-431cec4908ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{84}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302087} :answer-field/id #uuid "57d6ae22-e3ea-5f1f-85d5-05dac214ce17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c86d0c2-70d5-57fc-875d-6cf845fb24e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-7469" :question/problem "Express $\\sqrt{5}-2\\sqrt{5}{sin}^{2}⁡{42}^{∘}$ as a single trigonometric ratio." :question/worked-solution "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5}(1-2{sin}^{2}⁡{42}^{∘})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n1-2{sin}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={42}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-2{sin}^{2}⁡{42}^{∘} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {42}^{∘})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡{84}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}(1-2{sin}^{2}⁡{42}^{∘}) & =\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{84}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262423 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2902b205-4508-55c6-9a68-f57d3afc9eab" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Values of Trigonometric Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53bf9521-dc3d-5ab7-92d1-eec6f21714f7" :answer/type {:db/